/* ia32 syscalls recorded for 32-bit Wine processes (the i386 unix side of old WoW64): MM_IA32(ia32 name, ia32
 * number, x86_64 name). bpf.cpp fills the kernel's ia32_nr map from it, so a record carries the x86_64 number
 * and the agent decodes it like a 64-bit call (MM_F_COMPAT). The ia32 numbers are those of <asm/unistd_32.h>;
 * the subcalls of the socketcall and ipc multiplexers (32-bit glibc makes its socket and SysV IPC calls through
 * them) are keyed MM_IA32_SOCKETCALL / MM_IA32_IPC + subcall, and monitor.bpf.c ia32_args unpacks their
 * arguments, and old_mmap's struct (90: Wine's i386 preloader maps with it). The 64-bit-offset, *_time64, 32-bit-uid
 * and old-stat variants map to the one x86_64 call. Only x86_64 calls kSyscalls records are listed; the numbers not
 * listed are kernel aggregates (sysagg.h), keyed by their ia32 number (as <asm/syscalls_32.h> dispatches it: fcntl
 * 55 runs compat_sys_fcntl64, as fcntl64 does). */
